    },
    {
      "label": "Regional systems",
      "kicker": "02 · The large polygons",
      "title": "Similar scale, different institutions",
      "text": "British Columbia uses regional districts; New Brunswick now uses Regional Service Commissions; Quebec has MRCs and equivalent territories; Ontario mixes counties, districts, regional municipalities, and united counties. Elsewhere, a census division may be only a statistical frame.",
      "focus": "Regional types across Canada",
      "visibleLayerIds": [
        "regional-2025"
